                <pb facs="0836" n="746" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/394: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >McMillin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-12T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Department’s April 11, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>You will impress upon Estrada Cabrera and upon the leaders of the Unionists the
                    importance of an immediate armistice and a conference in order that the lives of
                    foreigners in Guatemala City may not be further endangered.</p>
                <p>You will intimate orally to the Unionists that whatever may be the result of the
                    conference they should proceed in strict accordance with the provisions of the
                    Constitution of Guatemala in order to ensure recognition of any future
                    government which may be formed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
